  "name": "Script-rolled proc talents fire at their tooltip chance, not its square (#4275)",
  "contract": "These auras roll their own proc chance in their AuraScript CheckProc, so their spell_proc.Chance must be 100. rev_20260919_20 set it to 0, which SpellMgr::LoadSpellProcs replaces with the DBC ProcChance, so Aura::GetProcEffectMask rolled the chance again after CheckProc and each proc fired at P x P (Umbral Glaive 10% became 1%, #4275). aura_proc_rate runs the aura's full proc decision (db filters, conditions, CheckProc and the native chance roll) 40000 times on a synthetic event of the shape the script expects; one talent per class event script. Each window is P +/- 1.5 points, at least 6 standard deviations wide, and excludes P x P. Deadly Neurotoxins rolls only for its Rotfang extension, so every qualifying crit must pass the decision.",
